---
title: Attachment lifecycle
---
flowchart TD
  plan([Exposure plan]) --> kinds[One ManagedArtifact per side effect<br/>a symlink, a vendor config entry,<br/>a region of a shared file, a hook entry,<br/>or one only its integration can read]
  kinds --> occupied{Is the name already taken?}
  occupied -->|no| attach[Attach: the owning integration writes it]
  occupied -->|taken, and it resolves to nothing| adopt[Adopt it: it delivers no capability,<br/>so refusing it preserves no work]
  occupied -->|taken, and it resolves| held[Preserve it, report the capability,<br/>and deliver the rest]
  adopt --> attach
  attach --> receipt[(A typed receipt in the ledger)]
  receipt --> inspect{Inspect the harness as it is now}
  inspect -->|it is as the receipt says| matched[MATCHED]
  inspect -->|it is gone| missing[MISSING]
  inspect -->|it changed under us| drifted[DRIFTED]
  inspect -->|someone else owns that name| conflict[CONFLICT]
  inspect -->|this build cannot verify it| blocked[BLOCKED]
  ledger[An unreadable ledger] --> blocked
  matched --> detach[Detach, and the harness stops carrying it]
  missing --> noop[Nothing to undo, and nothing is claimed]
  drifted --> refuse[Refuse the mutation, and report what was found]
  conflict --> refuse
  blocked --> refuse
  sweep[/uze doctor: a reference into UZE's own home<br/>that resolves to nothing and no receipt claims/] --> remove[Remove it: nothing else writes there,<br/>so it can only be UZE's own leftover]
